From: mscharged-port
Subject: Dawn skips its command validation
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host performance. Apply after 0126.

Dawn validates every command on the render thread before it records it for
the driver (about a third of the render thread's time in a match). Dawn's
skip_validation toggle is now set unless the backend debug layers are on:
the recorded driver commands are the same, robust buffer and shader access
stay on. Owner decision 2026-11-13 (earlier builds kept validation).

diff --git a/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp b/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
index bbf9999..61f7659 100644
--- a/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
+++ b/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
@@ -1045,6 +1045,11 @@ bool initialize(AuroraBackend auroraBackend, bool allowCpu) {
     // spirv-val of Tint's output is a debug check, run on every pipeline even
     // when the blob cache hits. It follows the backend debug layers.
     if (!g_config.enableBackendValidation) disableToggles.push_back("enable_spirv_validation");
+    // Without the backend debug layers Dawn does not validate every command on
+    // the render thread. The commands it records for the driver are the same;
+    // robust buffer and shader access stay on (they change generated code,
+    // validation does not).
+    if (!g_config.enableBackendValidation) enableToggles.push_back("skip_validation");
     wgpu::DawnTogglesDescriptor togglesDescriptor(wgpu::DawnTogglesDescriptor::Init{
         .nextInChain = &cacheDescriptor,
         .enabledToggleCount = enableToggles.size(),
